  "id": "integrated-system",
  "term": "integrated system",
  "definition": "An integrated system is a research tool used to assess quality of life in people with cancer who are taking part in clinical trials or other studies. It brings together measures of daily functioning, common symptoms, overall health and quality of life, and selected individual concerns such as sleep, appetite, bowel problems, breathing, and financial difficulties.",
